{"name":"Lover’s Leap","hex":"#957e68","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lover","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who loves and cares for another person in a romantic way; a sweetheart, love, soulmate, boyfriend, girlfriend, or spouse.","A sexual partner, especially one with whom someone is having an affair."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Obsolete form of louver."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lover"},{"term":"leap","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To jump.","To pass over by a leap or jump."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of leaping or jumping.","The distance traversed by a leap or jump."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leap"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lover's Leap","blocks":[{"text":"Lover's Leap, or Lovers' Leap, is a toponym given to a number of locations of varying height, usually isolated, with the risk of a fatal fall and the possibility of a deliberate jump. Legends of romantic tragedy are often associated with a Lover's Leap."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Hawks_Nest.JPG/330px-Hawks_Nest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lover's_Leap","wikidata":"Q6692322"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Two_Lover%27s_Point_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Two_Lover%27s_Point_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Two_Lover%27s_Point_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-Two_Lover%27s_Point_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Two_Lover%27s_Point_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Two_Lover%27s_Point_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two Lovers Point is a major tourist attracti